{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>When a man steals.</b> R. Yeshuah said: HaShem added to the penalty for the ox more than for the sheep, because one cannot conceal an ox as one can a sheep, and none can steal it except one more practiced in the craft of theft, and the Gaon [Saadia] said: because of the loss that will come to the ox's owner more than the sheep, for with it he plows."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:14.626563617Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}